# Prospective option-resumption metadata interface amendment r1

Actual author: `/root`, 2026-10-10 UTC. Apply this NEW amendment together with the preserved metadata draft `RSM_OPTION_RESUMPTION_METADATA_V1.md` (SHA256 `1612b14d7549b7fb406cbef8e127440dcfddaf30548ef29d217bc49aefb6c854`). Where their interface statements differ, this amendment is operative. The original draft and root freeze `ab948541d137ec679562f61309b2192277da65f45266cd80443187e06c07b3b0` remain immutable. No checker or producer used the draft before this correction. This amendment responds to the actual public design review `4a66727f7839ef6d6cf91bd0fafd6999feffd497078dcda6d3f0bc726317ba06` and the formal engineer's separate read-only review. It changes no task semantics, control meaning, proposed source index, split or cohort size. It approves no data.

## Claim container, identifiers and compatible diagnostics

Use the established canonical field `family_control_claims`. The draft's `family_claims` spelling is superseded; the future checker must reject a parallel ignored alias. There is one claim for each of the nine required supplied controls on every actual record. Required fields are `scope`, `evidence_manifest`, `control_id`, ordered `pair_sample_ids`, and at least one identifier field `name` or `property`. An identifier is a literal string from the published nine-name table. If both are present, both must be strings with equal values; they do not define two claims. Normalize this identifier choice only for lookup. Do not coerce scalar values, semantic tasks or member order.

The claim vocabulary also permits these optional, typed provenance/diagnostic fields: `source_family_key` (string), `source_family_index` (integer excluding boolean), `controlled_context` (one published context), `renderer` (forward/reverse), `pair_record_hashes` (ordered two-string SHA256 list), and `diagnostics` (JSON object). Optional provenance coordinates and member hashes must agree with the actual owner/resolved members. Diagnostics are untrusted annotations, with no power to override or replace any required relationship. Other claim fields require a separately published amendment; the superseded exact six-key restriction does not apply. A probe locator cannot stand in for actual pair IDs. The finite nine-name set and exactly one required claim per name remain the initial cohort's explicit completeness requirements.

For the first eight controls, owner and both members share actual source family/index/split/renderer; nonmember owners are legitimate. For `object_field_order_invariance`, both members instead share the owner's actual family/index/split/context and are ordered forward,reverse. The owner is either of those members. Do not require both field-order members to share the owner's renderer. Recursive object-field presentation may differ only within that actual same-context pair, and every list order/type/value remains fixed. No field-order equality is asserted across different contexts.

## Manifest fields and external byte inputs

The minimal top-level manifest fields are `metadata_version` (integer 1 excluding boolean), `batch` (the configured proposed batch), `candidate_sha256` (actual complete PENDING candidate byte SHA256), `source_bindings`, and `control_pairs`. Additional top-level and entry diagnostics remain permitted. All `evidence_manifest` paths resolve from the dataset factory root; reject absolute paths, parent traversal and symlink components. Claims identify a supplied file, not an ambient or network resource.

`source_bindings` maps safe factory-relative public paths to lowercase 64-character SHA256 strings. It contains the actual byte hashes of all five operative public files: the unchanged task contract, curriculum, configuration, preserved metadata draft and this amendment. A caller supplies and verifies those actual public bytes; additional source bindings may be preserved but must be truthful if asserted. The named paths are:

- `schemas/RSM_OPTION_RESUMPTION_V1.md`
- `research/curricula/RSM-OPTION-RESUMPTION-PROSPECTIVE-20261010.md`
- `research/curricula/RSM-OPTION-RESUMPTION-CONFIG-20261010.json`
- `schemas/RSM_OPTION_RESUMPTION_METADATA_V1.md`
- `schemas/RSM_OPTION_RESUMPTION_METADATA_V1_AMENDMENT_R1.md`

Each `control_pairs` entry retains the draft's coordinate/hash/member minimum fields, except that its identifier accepts the same name/property rule. Resolve by `(control_id,normalized identifier,ordered actual pair IDs)` to exactly one named entry. Shared IDs across different names remain valid; duplicates of the complete lookup key fail. Validate actual full member record hashes independently whether optional hashes are supplied or omitted.

The checker receives raw manifest bytes as a supplied ledger and reports their externally frozen actual hashes. **Do not require a manifest SHA inside candidate claims:** a manifest already contains the candidate SHA, so embedding the manifest's SHA back into the candidate would create circular custody. Accepted-release checking receives the preserved original PENDING candidate bytes and joins their full records to accepted projections, allowing only the established review-status/receipt/lineage hash changes. Do not substitute reserialized accepted records for the exact original candidate file. Missing candidate, manifest, operative public-source or target-free legacy input bytes produce UNKNOWN/failure for their required custody/control/novelty gates.

## Typed witnesses, difficulty and actual dependencies

`property_witnesses` is a JSON object, possibly empty, containing optional diagnostics. Supported optional locator keys are `saved_binding_locator` and `checkpoint_tamper_locator` (lists of literal object keys or integer list indices, excluding boolean indices, rooted at the actual R checkpoint), and `replay_locator` (object with exactly `option,body_path,index`, locating an actual declared primitive instruction). Supported optional metrics under `dependency_metrics` are nonnegative integers named `maximum_option_depth`, `maximum_selected_branch_depth`, `declared_instructions`, `total_F_events`, `total_F_effects`, `history_effects_at_R`, `caller_frames_at_R`, and `selected_branch_frames_at_R`. Recompute supplied metric/locator facts. Additional private narrative diagnostics may appear inside `diagnostics` (object); no unpublished row-property vocabulary, mandatory proof annotation or required locator is inferred. Required family relationships are reconstructed even when witnesses are absent.

Canonical `difficulty` and `structural_difficulty` are strict integers 2..4 and agree. A nonempty `source_provenance.curriculum_difficulty_explanation` string explains actual instruction, retained-frame, argument, guard and continuation dependencies. The checker can confirm typed structure and supplied measured facts; independent review assesses whether the explanation supports the level. Neither a context label, a frame/event count alone, nor a longer prompt determines difficulty. Invalid-control contexts may still require validating the supplied program and original committed history; zero new effects do not make their verification automatically trivial.

All stronger unchanged curriculum obligations apply to the same actual programs: at R a retained nonroot option's current initiation is false after it previously entered successfully; an actually selected branch remains selected after its current guard becomes false; nested caller work and an immutable register-derived argument remain pending and that saved argument affects later execution. Both controls and derived metrics use the actual active frame and its binding copy. The decisive changed I initiation atom has all other initiation atoms true; the S changed root-success atom has all other root-success atoms true. Respect configured event/instruction/argument/option/range bounds and the original mode/budget/history policies. P must commit a new effect and leave semantic work; pending return work suffices, and no extra future-effect requirement is added.

For A, changing an unused parameter's enter-event binding alone is insufficient. Independently identify an actual later effect operand, evaluated guard or success computation depending on the changed root argument, with both runs completing and an actual behavior difference.

For replay, match an actually committed original effect and an actually executed T new effect by the declared option and body instruction locator. Restart invocation counters and after-states may differ. Let g be the original primitive's exact state transformation with original invocation bindings retained and register expressions evaluated against each successive state. Its original pre-state s must satisfy g(g(s)) != g(s), and T must actually execute that same instruction again after successful root initiation. This rejects zero additions, identity/idempotent scales and swaps on equal operands. Terminal state or status and continuation traces must also differ as already required; merely naming a primitive non-idempotent or pointing at blocked code does not pass.

X changes exactly one actual active state/cursor/binding scalar, while keeping the original history and other task fields fixed, and is rejected at invalid_checkpoint before any event. A saved-binding locator must point to the particular retained frame copy read by pending work, rather than another option/branch copy that happens to share a parameter name. Its changed value must affect a future evaluated operand/predicate/event/state in a diagnostic continuation of that modified trusted machine. A cursor change must alter pending instruction/return selection; a state change must affect a subsequent read or observable continuation state before being overwritten. Such counterfactual machine diagnostics are evidence of activity, never permission to accept the invalid supplied checkpoint. No mere invocation-counter, inactive binding or unused metadata tamper substitutes for X.

## Public graph normalization and remaining boundary

Before production compare all actual proposed F programs with each other and the actual target-free legacy source inputs. Use a full-option view retaining ordered instructions/calls/branches, guard and success predicates, parameter declaration and def/use dependencies, register read/write roles, and entry/root identity. Alpha-canonicalize option/parameter/register names and erase numeric literal values, renderer/ID/context spelling, initial numeric state, history, checkpoints and cuts/budgets. Preserve operator/comparison and dependency structure.

Also compare two deliberately coarser shared-primitive views: drop option initiation/success/argument wrappers and root marking, collapse constants and parameter operands to scalar operands, and retain ordered add/scale/swap writes, live-register reads, comparisons, branches and procedure calls. One includes all declared procedures; one includes those syntactically reachable from the entry through both branches. Lift legacy procedures/main into equivalent procedure graphs, alpha-canonicalize names/register roles and erase literal values. Require all twelve actual programs to be distinct and have no legacy collision in each view. This stronger coarse check prevents unused padding, constant/name changes or merely introducing option syntax from inflating source counts. Report actual legacy signature collapse separately from lineage-family counts. Handwritten feasibility novelty is insufficient for the later actual producer cohort.

The prospective 216 correlated views, 108 typed control tasks, 300 named pairs and 1,944 owner claims are unchanged arithmetic; 1,344 of the first eight controls' claims have nonmember owners. All counts remain ungenerated here. Freeze the five public files and independent checker source/fixtures/tests before first execution, preserve all first failures, and use complete prospective positive/negative fixtures. Whole-cohort expert/red predictions before gold, separate first judgments, adjudication, immutable release validation and fresh remote-byte verification remain later gates. Public-design/review/adjudication overlap, common-model risk, feasibility reuse, finite-program shortcuts and exposed development data remain disclosed; no model training or efficacy is claimed.
